Feature: Launching
  Pick what to start on the LAUNCH screen, then click LAUNCH. GROUND STATION starts the sim,
  ArduPilot SITL and the console together. SIMULATOR ONLY starts the sim alone. WITH ARDUPILOT
  flies the T1-S VTOL. WITHOUT ARDUPILOT flies the plain T1-S Ranger in the sim. In the
  station, WITHOUT ARDUPILOT gives the sticks to the sim's own modes, and ArduPilot only
  reports. TOWERS starts the commander app of [[Towers]] on a game of your own, in the valley
  of the game: you command Blue, and Red is the computer, or nobody for a practice game.
  DRONE CAMERAS turns the 3D view of the game, and the pictures from the drones, on or off.
  The launcher opens on the station with ArduPilot, in the Alpine Valley.

  [[Running and stopping a program]] tells you what LAUNCH does next.

  Expectation: SIMULATOR ONLY picks the sim alone
    Given the launch target is not SIMULATOR ONLY
    When the launch target is SIMULATOR ONLY
    Then the launch target is SIMULATOR ONLY

  Expectation: GROUND STATION picks the station
    Given the launch target is not GROUND STATION
    When the launch target is GROUND STATION
    Then the launch target is GROUND STATION

  Expectation: TOWERS picks the commander app
    Given the launch target is not TOWERS
    When the launch target is TOWERS
    Then the launch target is TOWERS

  Expectation: WITH ARDUPILOT picks the flight controller
    Given the flight controller choice is WITHOUT ARDUPILOT
    When the flight controller choice is WITH ARDUPILOT
    Then the flight controller choice is WITH ARDUPILOT

  Expectation: WITHOUT ARDUPILOT picks the plain plane
    Given the flight controller choice is WITH ARDUPILOT
    When the flight controller choice is WITHOUT ARDUPILOT
    Then the flight controller choice is WITHOUT ARDUPILOT

  Expectation: LAUNCH starts the station with ArduPilot
    Hands over to: the console is connected to a plane on the ground
    Given the launch target is GROUND STATION
    And the flight controller choice is WITH ARDUPILOT
    When the pilot launches
    Then the program in the log is the ground station
    And the sticks of the started station are through ArduPilot

  Expectation: Without ArduPilot, the station gives the sticks to the sim
    The sim flies the plane through its own modes. ArduPilot still runs, for the telemetry,
    but the sim does not use its outputs.

    Given the launch target is GROUND STATION
    And the flight controller choice is WITHOUT ARDUPILOT
    When the pilot launches
    Then the program in the log is the ground station
    And the sticks of the started station are direct

  Expectation: The sim alone with ArduPilot flies the T1-S VTOL
    The sim starts its own ArduPilot: the native build, or the Docker image.

    Hands over to: the sim has just started with a flight controller
    Given the launch target is SIMULATOR ONLY
    And the flight controller choice is WITH ARDUPILOT
    When the pilot launches
    Then the program in the log is the simulator
    And the plane of the started sim is the T1-S VTOL

  Expectation: The sim alone without ArduPilot flies the T1-S Ranger
    Hands over to: the sim has just started
    Given the launch target is SIMULATOR ONLY
    And the flight controller choice is WITHOUT ARDUPILOT
    When the pilot launches
    Then the program in the log is the simulator
    And the plane of the started sim is the T1-S Ranger

  Expectation: The place goes to the program
    Given the place choice is CYPRESS
    When the pilot launches
    Then the place of the started program is Cypress

  Expectation: RAY TRACING goes to the program
    Given the ray tracing choice is on
    When the pilot launches
    Then the ray tracing of the started program is on

  Expectation: TOWERS starts a game of Towers against the computer
    The commander app starts the game server with six ArduPlane drones and takes the Blue seat.
    It needs the AGENT build of ArduPlane.

    Hands over to: a game of Towers is in play
    Given the launch target is TOWERS
    When the pilot launches
    Then the program in the log is the Towers game
    And the Red team of the started game is the computer
    And the drone cameras of the started game are on

  Expectation: RED: NOBODY makes a practice game
    Overrides: TOWERS starts a game of Towers against the computer

    Given the launch target is TOWERS
    And the Red team is NOBODY
    When the pilot launches
    Then the program in the log is the Towers game
    And the Red team of the started game is nobody

  Expectation: DRONE CAMERAS off starts the game with no 3D view
    Overrides: TOWERS starts a game of Towers against the computer

    Given the launch target is TOWERS
    And the drone cameras choice is off
    When the pilot launches
    Then the program in the log is the Towers game
    And the drone cameras of the started game are off
